    "proof_tex": "Fix a declared comparator and write \\(b=b^{\\mathrm{cmp}}\\).  Both \\(b\\) and \\(b^\\star(X)\\) satisfy \\(A'b=\\omega\\).  Every coordinate of \\(\\Psi\\) in target block \\(k\\) has conditional mean \\(h_k(X)\\), so both aggregate scores have conditional mean \\(\\omega'h(X)\\).  Put \\(d=b-b^\\star=Nz\\).  Lemma \\(\\ref{lem:singular-operator}\\) gives \\(N'\\Gamma b^\\star=0\\), whence\n\\[\nb'\\Gamma b-b^{\\star\\prime}\\Gamma b^\\star\n=2d'\\Gamma b^\\star+d'\\Gamma d=d'\\Gamma d=z'Hz.\n\\tag{E7}\n\\]\nThe conditional variance formula and integration prove (E1).  The identities\n\\[\nV_{\\mathrm{agg}}-V_{\\mathrm{can}}=\\Delta_{\\mathrm{normal}},\n\\qquad\nV_{\\mathrm{can}}-V_{\\mathrm{OVS}}=\\Delta_{\\mathrm{model}}\n\\]\nfrom Theorem \\(\\ref{thm:complete-normal-canonical-gradient}\\) then prove (E2)--(E3).\n\nMoreover,\n\\[\nN'\\Gamma b=N'\\Gamma(b-b^\\star)=Hz.\n\\tag{E8}\n\\]\nIf (E8) is zero, then (E7) is zero.  Conversely, if the expectation of (E7) is zero, nonnegativity gives \\(z'H(X)z=0\\) almost surely.  Positive semidefiniteness implies \\(H(X)z=0\\), so (E8) vanishes.  This proves (E4), including singular cases.\n\nThe difference \\(b'\\Psi-\\psi_P^0\\) is a measurable clean-comparison contrast and belongs to\n\\[\n\\mathcal C_P\\subseteq\\mathcal T_P^\\perp\n\\subseteq\\mathcal T_{P,\\mathrm{OVS}}^\\perp\n\\]\nby Theorem \\(\\ref{thm:observable-equivalence}\\).  Therefore \\(b'\\Psi\\) is an ambient gradient of the same target in both observed models.  An ambient gradient has variance equal to a model's canonical bound exactly when its projection onto that model's tangent orthocomplement is zero.  Tangent exhaustion gives\n\\[\n\\mathcal T_P^\\perp\n=\\overline{\\{a(X)'Z_P^{\\mathrm{per}}\\}},\n\\qquad\n\\mathcal T_{P,\\mathrm{OVS}}^\\perp\n=\\overline{\\{a(X)'Z_P^{\\mathrm{OVS}}\\}}.\n\\tag{E9}\n\\]\nOrthogonality to every measurable multiple in (E9) is equivalent, by conditional expectation, to (E5) and (E6), respectively.  This proves the two remaining equivalences and the interpretation of the three diagnostics.",
    "justification": "Three observable residuals distinguish aggregate optimality, localized-model efficiency, and published OVS efficiency.",
    "gap": "Neither the aggregate KKT equation nor the localized normal equation alone certifies equality with the published bound.",
    "consumer": "The optional \\(\\texttt{triplediff}\\) backend can report all three diagnostics without conflating their meanings.",
